-- State Pension Regulations 2015 (S.I. 2015/173) -- PART 7 (Overseas Residents): regulations 21 to 23.
-- Source: plain-text rendering of legislation.gov.uk, version 2026-04-06 (uksi-2015-173.txt); not the official text.
--
-- Parent-law and other-instrument effects taken as stated inputs, never guessed:
--   * whether a person is an "overseas resident" (a term of the 2014 Act, not defined in these Regulations);
--   * whether "Regulations are made ... which provide that this regulation applies to that up-rating increase"
--     (regulation 21(2)(a)): regulation 21 does nothing to an increase unless they are, and they are not among the inputs.
--   * the weekly rate "to which the person would have been entitled ... if the person's entitlement had not been deferred",
--     at the start and at the end of a part of the deferral period (regulation 22).

§ `Part 7 -- Overseas Residents`

§§ `Regulation 21: up-rating increases`

-- Paragraph (6): the territory specified is any part of the Channel Islands that is not subject to an Order under section 179 of
-- the Administration Act.
-- src:295 | (6) For the purposes of sections 18(4) and 20(2) and (3) of the 2014 Act, the territory specified is any part of the Channel Islands which is not subject to an Order made under section 179 of the Administration Act.
@ref Regulation 21(6) (src:295)
GIVEN `the person is in a part of the Channel Islands` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that part is subject to an Order made under section 179 of the Administration Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the person is in a territory specified in regulation 21(6)` `the person is in a part of the Channel Islands` `given` `that part is subject to an Order made under section 179 of the Administration Act` MEANS
        `the person is in a part of the Channel Islands`
    AND (NOT `that part is subject to an Order made under section 179 of the Administration Act`)

-- Paragraph (2): regulation 21 bites only if Regulations are made that say it applies to the up-rating increase. Paragraph (3): the
-- deferral case. Paragraph (4): in that case, which increases are lost. Paragraph (5): in all other cases, an overseas resident who
-- was entitled immediately before the increase loses it. Paragraph (1) is the rule these paragraphs elaborate.
-- "At the time of that increase" (paragraph (4)) and "immediately before the up-rating increase comes into force" (paragraph (5))
-- are read as the same moment (fork F19).
-- src:276 | (1) An overseas resident who is entitled to a state pension under Part 1 of the 2014 Act is not entitled to up-rating increases in accordance with this regulation.
-- src:277 | (2) This regulation—
-- src:278 | (a) applies in relation to an up-rating increase if Regulations are made—
-- src:279 | (i) in consequence of an order under section 150A (annual up-rating) or 151A of the Administration Act or in consequence of any other legislation; and
-- src:280 | (ii) which provide that this regulation applies to that up-rating increase; and
-- src:281 | (b) is subject to the Regulations made as mentioned in sub-paragraph (a).
-- src:282 | (3) Paragraph (4) applies in a case where—
-- src:283 | (a) a person’s entitlement to a state pension under Part 1 of the 2014 Act has been deferred for a period; and
-- src:284 | (b) when the deferral period ends, that person is—
-- src:285 | (i) entitled to a state pension under Part 1 of the 2014 Act; and
-- src:286 | (ii) an overseas resident.
-- src:287 | (4) Where this paragraph applies, the person mentioned in paragraph (3) is not entitled to any up-rating increases—
-- src:288 | (a) in respect of the deferral period if—
-- src:289 | (i) the person was an overseas resident at the time of that increase; and
-- src:290 | (ii) the person continued to be an overseas resident until the deferral period ended; and
-- src:291 | (b) after the deferral period ended if the person is an overseas resident at the time of that increase.
-- src:292 | (5) In all other cases, a person is not entitled to up-rating increases where, immediately before the up-rating increase comes into force, they were—
-- src:293 | (a) entitled to a state pension under Part 1 of the 2014 Act; and
-- src:294 | (b) an overseas resident.
@ref Regulation 21(1), 21(2), 21(3), 21(4), 21(5) (src:276-294)
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Facts about an up-rating increase for a person abroad`
GIVETH A `What regulation 21 does to an up-rating increase`
`what regulation 21 does to an up-rating increase` `the facts` MEANS
    IF   NOT (`the facts`'s `Regulations have been made providing that regulation 21 applies to the up-rating increase`)
    THEN `regulation 21 does not apply to this increase, because no Regulations have been made applying it`
    ELSE IF   `the person is deprived of the increase`
         THEN `regulation 21 takes the increase away from the person`
         ELSE `regulation 21 does not take the increase away from the person`
    WHERE
        `the deferral case applies` MEANS
                `the facts`'s `the person's entitlement to a state pension had been deferred for a period`
            AND `the facts`'s `when the deferral period ended the person was entitled to a state pension under Part 1 of the 2014 Act`
            AND `the facts`'s `when the deferral period ended the person was an overseas resident`
        `the person is deprived of the increase` MEANS
            IF   `the deferral case applies`
            THEN (    (    `the facts`'s `where the increase falls against the deferral period` EQUALS `in respect of the deferral period`
                       AND `the facts`'s `the person was an overseas resident at the time of the increase`
                       AND `the facts`'s `the person continued to be an overseas resident until the deferral period ended`)
                  OR  (    `the facts`'s `where the increase falls against the deferral period` EQUALS `after the deferral period ended`
                       AND `the facts`'s `the person was an overseas resident at the time of the increase`))
            ELSE     `the facts`'s `the person was entitled to a state pension under Part 1 of the 2014 Act immediately before the increase`
                 AND `the facts`'s `the person was an overseas resident at the time of the increase`

§§ `Regulation 22: the amount of an increment`

-- Paragraph (1): the regulation applies when, during any part of the deferral period, the person has been an overseas resident.
-- ("Subject to regulation 23" is regulation 23's own rule, below.)
-- src:297 | (1) Subject to regulation 23, this regulation applies in cases where, during any part of the deferral period, a person has been an overseas resident.
@ref Regulation 22(1) (src:297)
GIVEN `the parts` IS A LIST OF `A part of the deferral period, abroad or not`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`regulation 22 applies to the deferral period` `the parts` MEANS
    any (GIVEN `a part` YIELD `a part`'s `the person was an overseas resident during the part`) `the parts`

-- Paragraph (2): an overseas resident not in Great Britain or a specified territory: the weekly rate immediately before the start of
-- the part. Paragraph (3): not an overseas resident: the weekly rate immediately before the end of the part. An overseas resident who
-- is in Great Britain or a specified territory is in neither paragraph.
-- src:298 | (2) For any part of the deferral period during which the person was an overseas resident and was not in Great Britain or a territory specified in regulation 21(6), section 17(4) of the 2014 Act is modified to provide that the amount of an increment is equal to a percentage specified in regulations of the weekly rate of the state pension to which the person would have been entitled immediately before the start of that part of the deferral period if the person’s entitlement had not been deferred.
-- src:299 | (3) For any part of the deferral period during which the person was not an overseas resident, section 17(4) of the 2014 Act is modified to provide that the amount of an increment is equal to a specified percentage of the weekly rate of the state pension to which the person would have been entitled immediately before the end of that part of the deferral period if the person’s entitlement had not been deferred.
@ref Regulation 22(2), 22(3) (src:298-299)
GIVEN `the part` IS A `A part of the deferral period, abroad or not`
GIVETH A `Which weekly rate an increment is a percentage of`
`which weekly rate the increment for a part is a percentage of` `the part` MEANS
    IF   NOT (`the part`'s `the person was an overseas resident during the part`)
    THEN `the weekly rate immediately before the end of the part`
    ELSE IF   `the part`'s `the person was in Great Britain or a territory specified in regulation 21(6) during the part`
         THEN `the Regulations do not say, because the person was an overseas resident who was in Great Britain or a specified territory`
         ELSE `the weekly rate immediately before the start of the part`

@ref Regulation 22(2), 22(3) (src:298-299)
GIVEN `the part` IS A `A part of the deferral period, abroad or not`
      `the weekly rate immediately before the start of the part` IS A NUMBER
      `the weekly rate immediately before the end of the part` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the weekly rate regulation 22 refers to for a part` `the part` `given the rate at the start` `the weekly rate immediately before the start of the part` `and the rate at the end` `the weekly rate immediately before the end of the part` MEANS
    CONSIDER `which weekly rate the increment for a part is a percentage of` `the part`
    WHEN `the weekly rate immediately before the start of the part` THEN JUST `the weekly rate immediately before the start of the part`
    WHEN `the weekly rate immediately before the end of the part` THEN JUST `the weekly rate immediately before the end of the part`
    WHEN `the Regulations do not say, because the person was an overseas resident who was in Great Britain or a specified territory` THEN NOTHING

@ref Regulation 22(2), 22(3) (src:298-299)
GIVEN `the weekly rate` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the increment under regulation 22, the weekly rate being` `the weekly rate` MEANS
    `the specified percentage for the increase in the weekly rate` TIMES `the weekly rate`

§§ `Regulation 23: where regulations 12A and 22 both apply`

-- Paragraph (4): regulation 12A(2) is read with "the weekly rate" replaced by the rate regulation 22 refers to for that part.
-- Paragraph (5): the increase or decrease of the increment as so determined is added to, or taken from, the increment from (3).
-- Taken literally the increment worked out under (4) equals the one under (3) (both are the percentage of the same rate), so the
-- change is nil (fork F20); the steps are kept apart so a reviewer can see where a different reading would enter.
-- src:303 | (3) The amount of the increment is first determined in accordance with the modifications set out in regulation 22.
-- src:304 | (4) The amount of the increment is then determined in accordance with the modifications set out in regulation 12A as if the reference in regulation 12A(2) to the weekly rate of the state pension were a reference to the weekly rate referred to in—
-- src:305 | (a) regulation 22(2), for any part of the deferral period during which the person was an overseas resident and was not in Great Britain or a territory specified in regulation 21(6); and
-- src:306 | (b) regulation 22(3), for any part of the deferral period during which the person was not an overseas resident.
-- src:307 | (5) Any increase or decrease of the increment as determined in accordance with paragraph (4) is then added to, or subtracted from, the amount of the increment as determined in accordance with paragraph (3).
@ref Regulation 23(3), 23(4), 23(5) (src:303-307)
GIVEN `the weekly rate regulation 22 refers to` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the increment under regulation 23, the weekly rate regulation 22 refers to being` `the weekly rate regulation 22 refers to` MEANS
    `the first increment` PLUS `the change in the increment`
    WHERE
        `the first increment` MEANS `the increment under regulation 22, the weekly rate being` `the weekly rate regulation 22 refers to`
        `the increment worked out under paragraph (4)` MEANS `the increment for each whole week of a modification period, the weekly rate being` `the weekly rate regulation 22 refers to`
        `the change in the increment` MEANS `the increment worked out under paragraph (4)` MINUS `the first increment`

-- src:301 | (1) This regulation applies in a case where section 17(4) of the 2014 Act falls to be modified under both regulations 12A and 22 at the same time.
-- src:302 | (2) Section 17(4) of the 2014 Act is modified to provide that the amount of an increment is determined as set out in the following paragraphs.
@ref Regulation 23(1), 23(2) (src:301-302)
GIVEN `the period` IS A `Deferral period`
      `the dates of the non-uprating changes, earliest first` IS A LIST OF DATE
      `the parts` IS A LIST OF `A part of the deferral period, abroad or not`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`regulation 23 applies to` `the period` `given the non-uprating changes` `the dates of the non-uprating changes, earliest first` `and the parts` `the parts` MEANS
        NOT (null (`the modification periods of a deferral period` `the period` `given the non-uprating changes` `the dates of the non-uprating changes, earliest first`))
    AND `regulation 22 applies to the deferral period` `the parts`
